The “Time in Default” variable applies only to the non-performing modeling segment, while all missing data relates to the performing modeling segment. The “Borrower BTL LTV” variable is relevant only to customers in the BTL segment across both performing and non-performing segments, with missing values arising from accounts outside the BTL segment. Due to the high proportion of missing data for this variable—caused by historical data gaps in the FDM and calculation errors—MDT replaced it with “borrower_btl_ltv_peak” from table DDEWS02P.DW85360_MoC_BORROWER_BTL_LTV. To address these issues, MDT revisited the CRDM tables used in the implementation logic for accurate LTV calculation and applied a MoC adjustment for differences in development and implementation logic (see QL#106).



